From 715ebafdaab63b41a0126b4519330e2a3bfc3a73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:30:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] server: replies written as messages to recipients split
 into reasoning, answer and tool calls

A tokenizer with <|start|>, <|message|>, <|eom|> and <|eot|> as single tokens and a chat template that writes
to=self messages (Muse Spark Open's) replies as messages to recipients. self is reasoning_content; user, commentary
and no recipient are content; any other recipient is a tool call whose <atem:function_calls> block becomes the
<tool_call><function=...> markup tool_parse and tool_stream already read, so its arguments take the tools' schema
types. While a reply streams, an unfinished header, a call message that has not closed and a partial marker are held
back, so every split extends the last and the finished split extends them all; the finished reply feeds the call
streamer once more, so a last call ended by the end token streams too. Harmony's tokenizers have no <|eom|> or
<|eot|>, so gpt-oss replies keep their channel split; tests cover both formats whole and streamed.
